{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1028","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Restore Array"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"While discussing a proper problem A for a Codeforces Round, Kostya created a cyclic array of positive integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$. Since the talk was long and not promising, Kostya created a new cyclic array $$$b_1, b_2, \\ldots, b_{n}$$$ so that $$$b_i = (a_i \\mod a_{i + 1})$$$, where we take $$$a_{n+1} = a_1$$$. Here $$$mod$$$ is the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Modulo_operation"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"modulo operation"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":". When the talk became interesting, Kostya completely forgot how array $$$a$$$ had looked like. Suddenly, he thought that restoring array $$$a$$$ from array $$$b$$$ would be an interesting problem (unfortunately, not A)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2 \\le n \\le 140582$$$) — the length of the array $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$b_1, b_2, \\ldots, b_{n}$$$ ($$$0 \\le b_i \\le 187126$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If it is possible to restore some array $$$a$$$ of length $$$n$$$ so that $$$b_i = a_i \\mod a_{(i \\mod n) + 1}$$$ holds for all $$$i = 1, 2, \\ldots, n$$$, print «"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"» in the first line and the integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ in the second line. All $$$a_i$$$ should satisfy $$$1 \\le a_i \\le 10^{18}$$$. We can show that if an answer exists, then an answer with such constraint exists as well."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It it impossible to restore any valid $$$a$$$, print «"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"» in one line."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can print each letter in any case (upper or lower)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n1 3 1 0\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"YES\n1 3 5 2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n4 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"NO\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$1 \\mod 3 = 1$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$3 \\mod 5 = 3$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$5 \\mod 2 = 1$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$2 \\mod 1 = 0$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"1028E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1028/problem/E"}